1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:02,000
Pellet or briquette.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,200
Both are pressed biomass,

3
00:00:04,367 --> 00:00:04,800
but they are

4
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,233
not the same product.

5
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,467
Pellets are small,

6
00:00:07,467 --> 00:00:08,333
about the size

7
00:00:08,333 --> 00:00:09,600
of a pencil stub.

8
00:00:09,867 --> 00:00:12,700
They flow easily and feed automatically,

9
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:14,067
which is why power plants

10
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:17,200
co-firing biomass mostly ask for pellets.

11
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:18,367
Briquettes are bigger,

12
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:19,600
like short logs.

13
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:21,933
They are popular with industrial boilers,

14
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:23,333
brick kilns and factories.

15
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:24,800
Pellets need finer,

16
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,633
drier raw material and more processing,

17
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:28,567
so a pellet plant

18
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:30,333
costs more to set up.

19
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,100
Briquette machines are simpler,

20
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:33,400
which makes them

21
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,400
an easier place to start.

22
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,333
So which one should you make?

23
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:39,233
It depends on two things.

24
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:40,667
The raw material you have,

25
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:42,900
and who is buying near you.

26
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:43,867
Pellet makers,

27
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:44,833
briquette makers,

28
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:46,733
and the buyers for both.

29
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,500
IndiaBiomass is bringing them together.
